cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WRRA-M 0.5, please cite this research note."
title: "WRRA-M 0.5: Information Load and Twist Gravity in a Finite Model"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Wonsik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4263-9772"
    email: "janefather@gmail.com"
version: "0.5"
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
url: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
abstract: >-
  WRRA-M 0.5 foregrounds information load and twist gravity while separating mass phenotypes from the upstream continuous
  geometric response in the B_C model branch. Expansion and twist coexist,
  while the executed sector is static twist stress. A calibrated response
  from the earlier WRRA Galactic Disk paper is actually evaluated for finite
  spherical motion, effective stress mass, and conditional lensing. The
  earlier Milky Way algebraic calculation is reproduced, and a homogeneous
  sixteen-channel carrier passes transport rank conditions while producing
  zero filter-selection gaps. Hidden energy-weighted information load is
  linked to twist and a conditional finite, boundaryless T3 gluing example.
  Individual state weights are not computed in 0.5; the full hidden fraction
  and its local clustering subset are explicitly distinguished. Editable
  calibrations and reproducible calculations are supplied.
keywords:
  - WRRA
  - Wonsik Reality Renderer Architecture
  - mass quantization
  - continuous gravity
  - twist stress
  - dark matter
  - finite boundaryless universe
  - common carrier
  - filter selection
  - conditional lensing

